raph of y = g(x) at P and Q", "x0": 0.5538461538461539, "y0": 0.3861693861693862, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.40015540015540013}, {"text": "respectively. Mark on your sketch the", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.40404040404040403, "x1": 0.47912087912087914, "y1": 0.4172494172494173}, {"text": "ordinates of P and Q. Shade the region R", "x0": 0.512087912087912, "y0": 0.40404040404040403, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.4172494172494173}, {"text": "bounded by y = g(x) and the line PQ.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.4211344211344211, "x1": 0.4879120879120879, "y1": 0.43434343434343436}, {"text": "(d) Prove that the area of R is (#2 \u2014 8log, 3) square units,", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.44522144522144524, "x1": 0.6681318681318681, "y1": 0.4630924630924631}, {"text": "3. (a) On a perticular island, twenty per cent of all turtles survive for four weeks", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.4801864801864802, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.5011655011655012}, {"text": "after hatching. Fifteen turtles hatch on the same day and are tagged for a study.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.5011655011655012, "x1": 0.8604395604395605, "y1": 0.5143745143745144}, {"text": "(i) (@) all fifteen turtles will survive the four weeks;", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.5275835275835276, "x1": 0.6120879120879121, "y1": 0.5423465423465423}, {"text": "(8) none of the turtles survives the four weeks.", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.5547785547785548, "x1": 0.5648351648351648, "y1": 0.567987567987568}, {"text": "(ii) Write down expressions for the probability that:", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.581973581973582, "x1": 0.6043956043956044, "y1": 0.5951825951825952}, {"text": "(a) no more than three turtles survive the four weeks;", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.6076146076146076, "x1": 0.6296703296703297, "y1": 0.6216006216006216}, {"text": "(A) at least three turtles survive the four weeks.", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.6355866355866356, "x1": 0.5747252747252747, "y1": 0.6487956487956488}, {"text": "(b) The population P of a town increases at a rate proportional to the number by", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.662004662004662, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.6752136752136753}, {"text": "which the town\u2019s population exceeds 1000. This can be expressed by the differential", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.679098679098679, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.6923076923076923}, {"text": "equation 42 = k(P \u2014 1000) where \u00a2 is the time in years and k is a constant.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.6907536907536908, "x1": 0.8120879120879121, "y1": 0.714063714063714}, {"text": "(i) By differentiation show that P = 1000+ where A is a constant, is a solution", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.7195027195027195, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.7412587412587412}, {"text": "of this equation.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.7412587412587412, "x1": 0.29120879120879123, "y1": 0.7544677544677545}, {"text": "(ii) The population of the town was 2500 at the start of 1970 and 3000 at the start", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.7684537684537684, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.7816627816627817}, {"text": "of 1985. Find its population at the start of the year 2000.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.7855477855477856, "x1": 0.656043956043956, "y1": 0.7987567987567987}, {"text": "(iii) During which year will the population reach 4000?", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.8111888111888111, "x1": 0.6373626373626373, "y1": 0.8251748251748252}, {"text": "4. (a) (i) Express 2 = V2 in a modulus-argument form.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.8430458430458431, "x1": 0.7, "y1": 0.8663558663558664}, {"text": "(ii) Hence write 2% in the form a+ ib, where a and b are real.", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.8733488733488733, "x1": 0.7, "y1": 0.8888888888888888}], [{"text": "24", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.08469308469308469, "x1": 0.16593406593406593, "y1": 0.09246309246309246}, {"text": "(b) (i) On an Argand diagram shade in the region R containing all points repre-", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.11577311577311578, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.13053613053613053}, {"text": "senting complex numbers z such that 1 < |2| <2 and % <argz <4.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.13286713286713286, "x1": 0.7527472527472527, "y1": 0.14840714840714841}, {"text": "(ii) In R mark with a dot the point K representing a complex number z. Clearly in-", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.1592851592851593, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.17249417249417248}, {"text": "dicate on your diagram the points M, N, P and Q representing the complex numbers", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.17637917637917638, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.1895881895881896}, {"text": "%,\u2014z, and 2z respectively.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.19036519036519037, "x1": 0.3945054945054945, "y1": 0.20823620823620823}, {"text": "(c) Show that the locus specified by 3|z \u2014 (4+ 4#)| = |z \u2014 (12 + is a circle.", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.21756021756021757, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.23154623154623155}, {"text": "Write down its radius and the co-ordinates of its centre. Draw a neat sketch of the", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.23543123543123542, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.24553224553224554}, {"text": "circle", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.25252525252525254, "x1": 0.1956043956043956, "y1": 0.26262626262626265}, {"text": "5. The hyperbola H has equation ry = 16.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.2867132867132867, "x1": 0.5274725274725275, "y1": 0.2999222999222999}, {"text": "(a) Sketch this hyperbola and indicate on your diagram the positions and co-", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.31157731157731156, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.32634032634032634}, {"text": "ordinates of all points at which the curve intersects the axes of symmetry.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.32944832944832947, "x1": 0.7978021978021979, "y1": 0.34265734265734266}, {"text": "(b) 4), where p > 0, and Q(4q, 4), where q > 0, are two distince arbitrary", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.35275835275835277, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.37218337218337216}, {"text": "points on H. Find the equation of the chord PQ.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.372960372960373, "x1": 0.5835164835164836, "y1": 0.3861693861693862}, {"text": "(c) Prove that the equation of the tangent at P is x + = 8p.", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.3978243978243978, "x1": 0.7153846153846154, "y1": 0.41181041181041184}, {"text": "(d) The tangents at P and Q inters", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.41647241647241645, "x1": 0.46593406593406594, "y1": 0.4405594405594406}, {"text": "at T. Find the co-ordinates of T.", "x0": 0.5, "y0": 0.42424242424242425, "x1": 0.789010989010989, "y1": 0.43434343434343436}, {"text": "(e) The chord PQ produced passes through the point N(0,8).", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.44988344988344986, "x1": 0.6978021978021978, "y1": 0.4630924630924631}, {"text": "(i) Find the equation of the locus of T.", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.47474747474747475, "x1": 0.4945054945054945, "y1": 0.4887334887334887}, {"text": "(ii) Give a geometrical description of this locus:", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.5003885003885004, "x1": 0.5659340659340659, "y1": 0.5135975135975136}, {"text": "6. A body of mass one kilogram is projected vertically upwards from the ground at", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.5345765345765345, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.5477855477855478}, {"text": "a speed of 20 metres per second. The particle is under the effect of both gravity and", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.5516705516705517, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.5648795648795649}, {"text": "at any time, has a magnitude of 7507, where v is the magnitude", "x0": 0.3208791208791209, "y0": 0.5641025641025641, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.5866355866355867}, {"text": "of the particle\u2019s velocity at that time.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.5858585858585859, "x1": 0.47802197802197804, "y1": 0.5990675990675991}, {"text": "In the following questions take the acceleration due to gravity to be 10 metres per", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.6114996114996115, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.6247086247086248}, {"text": "second per second.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.6285936285936286, "x1": 0.3120879120879121, "y1": 0.6418026418026418}, {"text": "(a) While the body is travelling upwards the equation of motion is", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.6534576534576535, "x1": 0.721978021978022, "y1": 0.6682206682206682}, {"text": "(10+", "x0": 0.7824175824175824, "y0": 0.6542346542346542, "x1": 0.8208791208791208, "y1": 0.6674436674436675}, {"text": "(i) Taking # =", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.6806526806526807, "x1": 0.27912087912087913, "y1": 0.6946386946386947}, {"text": "calculate the greatest height reached by the particle.", "x0": 0.33186813186813185, "y0": 0.6814296814296814, "x1": 0.7912087912087912, "y1": 0.6946386946386947}, {"text": "4. calculate the time taken to reach this greatest height.", "x0": 0.2945054945054945, "y0": 0.7062937062937062, "x1": 0.7956043956043956, "y1": 0.7233877233877234}, {"text": "(ii) Taking #", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.7086247086247086, "x1": 0.26483516483516484, "y1": 0.7218337218337219}, {"text": "(b) Having reached its greatest height the particle fal", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.7342657342657343, "x1": 0.6252747252747253, "y1": 0.7474747474747475}, {"text": "to its starting point. The", "x0": 0.6527472527472528, "y0": 0.7342657342657343, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.7474747474747475}, {"text": "particle is still under the effect of both gravity and a r", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.7513597513597513, "x1": 0.6263736263736264, "y1": 0.7645687645687645}, {"text": "tance which, at any time,", "x0": 0.6582417582417582, "y0": 0.7513597513597513, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.7645687645687645}, {"text": "has a magnitude of 4,02", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.7661227661227661, "x1": 0.3626373626373626, "y1": 0.7832167832167832}, {"text": "(i) Write down the equation of motion of the particle as it falls.", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.7933177933177933, "x1": 0.710989010989011, "y1": 0.8073038073038074}, {"text": "(ii) Find the speed of the particle when it returns to its starting point.", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.8197358197358198, "x1": 0.7736263736263737, "y1": 0.8329448329448329}], [{"text": "25", "x0": 0.8648351648351649, "y0": 0.08469308469308469, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.09246309246309246}, {"text": "7. (a) (i) not", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.14918414918414918, "x1": 0.6230769230769231, "y1": 0.16472416472416473}, {"text": "ic", "x0": 0.5758241758241758, "y0": 0.16783216783216784, "x1": 0.5868131868131868, "y1": 0.17637917637917638}, {"text": "\u2014\u20142", "x0": 0.310989010989011, "y0": 0.19502719502719504, "x1": 0.5098901098901099, "y1": 0.20745920745920746}, {"text": "k 1 |", "x0": 0.3087912087912088, "y0": 0.2773892773892774, "x1": 0.7714285714285715, "y1": 0.3146853146853147}, {"text": "bp", "x0": 0.3384615384615385, "y0": 0.31934731934731936, "x1": 0.34945054945054943, "y1": 0.3418803418803419}, {"text": "A trapezium HIJK has parallel sides KJ = 16 cm and HI = 20 cm. The distance", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.351981351981352, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.3651903651903652}, {"text": "between these si m. L lies on HK and M lies on IJ such that LM is parallel", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.3690753690753691, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.3822843822843823}, {"text": "to KJ. The shortest nce from K to LM is h cm and LM has length \u00ab cm.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.3861693861693862, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.39937839937839936}, {"text": "Prove that \u00ab =", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.40326340326340326, "x1": 0.2813186813186813, "y1": 0.4133644133644134}, {"text": "(i) Figure not", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.43745143745143744, "x1": 0.5703296703296703, "y1": 0.4592074592074592}, {"text": "to scale", "x0": 0.42857142857142855, "y0": 0.46464646464646464, "x1": 0.5274725274725275, "y1": 0.47863247863247865}, {"text": "/", "x0": 0.5362637362637362, "y0": 0.6487956487956488, "x1": 0.5692307692307692, "y1": 0.6884226884226884}, {"text": "The diagram above is of a cake tin with a rectangular base with sides of 16 cm and", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.710955710955711, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.7241647241647242}, {"text": "10 cm. Its top is also rectangular with dimensions 20 cm and 12 cm. The tin has", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.728049728049728, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.7412587412587412}, {"text": "depth 4 cm and each of its four side faces is a trapezium. Find its volume.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.7451437451437452, "x1": 0.798901098901099, "y1": 0.7583527583527584}], [{"text": "26", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.08469308469308469, "x1": 0.16593406593406593, "y1": 0.09246309246309246}, {"text": "(b)", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.13131313131313133, "x1": 0.17912087912087912, "y1": 0.1445221445221445}, {"text": "ABCD is a cyclic quadrilateral. BA and CD are both produced and intersect at", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.445998445998446, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.4592074592074592}, {"text": "E. BC and AD produced intersect at F. The circles EAD, FCD intersect at G as", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.45454545454545453, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.48096348096348096}, {"text": "well as at D. Prove that the points and F are collinear", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.4716394716394716, "x1": 0.6813186813186813, "y1": 0.49805749805749805}, {"text": "8. (a) H 0", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.5322455322455323, "x1": 0.7703296703296704, "y1": 0.5547785547785548}, {"text": "A building is in the shape of a square prism with base edge \u00a2 metres and height", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.8585858585858586, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.8717948717948718}, {"text": "h metres. It stands on level ground. A base diagonal AC is produced to a point", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.8756798756798757, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.8888888888888888}], [{"text": "27", "x0": 0.8648351648351649, "y0": 0.08469308469308469, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.09246309246309246}, {"text": "K. From K it is found that the angles of elevation of F and G are 30\u00b0 and 45\u00b0", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.10878010878010878, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.1351981351981352}, {"text": "respectively. Prove that = TO |", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.1282051282051282, "x1": 0.4824175824175824, "y1": 0.14918414918414918}, {"text": "(b) Newton\u2019s method may be used to determine numerical approximations to the", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.16083916083916083, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.17404817404817405}, {"text": "real roots of the equation x? = 2.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.17793317793317792, "x1": 0.44065934065934065, "y1": 0.19114219114219114}, {"text": "Let 1 = be a series of estimations obtained by iterative appli-", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.20357420357420358, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.21678321678321677}, {"text": "cations of Newton\u2019s method.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.22066822066822067, "x1": 0.3989010989010989, "y1": 0.23076923076923078}, {"text": "(i) Show that 2,41 = a(en + x):", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.24087024087024086, "x1": 0.4582417582417582, "y1": 0.2665112665112665}, {"text": "(ii) Show algebraically that \u2014 Y2= 92)", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.2742812742812743, "x1": 0.6868131868131868, "y1": 0.30691530691530694}, {"text": "(iii) Given that > 2, show that ans \u2014 V2 < (an \u2014", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.3185703185703186, "x1": 0.6494505494505495, "y1": 0.33644133644133645}, {"text": "